    "overviewDetail": "The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia is rapidly emerging as a leading business destination in the Middle East, driven by its Vision 2030 economic diversification strategy. The country offers a large domestic market, strong government-backed infrastructure, and increasing openness to foreign investment across multiple sectors.\nSaudi Arabia has significantly streamlined its business setup processes through digital platforms, allowing faster company incorporation and licensing. Foreign investors can now own 100% of businesses in many sectors, supported by regulatory reforms aimed at improving ease of doing business. The Ministry of Investment (MISA) plays a central role in facilitating foreign direct investment and simplifying approval procedures.\nWith competitive corporate tax rates, access to government incentives, and major investments in sectors such as technology, tourism, and manufacturing, Saudi Arabia provides strong growth potential. Its strategic location connecting Asia, Europe, and Africa further strengthens its appeal for regional and global expansion",
